{
    "background_story": "Kimberly was a fiery and charismatic chef who owned a quaint French bistro in the heart of the city. Her culinary skills were matched only by her passion for cooking, and her signature dish was the infamous 'Flambe au Cognac'. With a flick of her wrist and a dash of drama, Kimberly would ignite the cognac, sending flames dancing across the plate. The spectacle never failed to impress her patrons, who would gather 'round to watch the show. But what they didn't know was that Kimberly's love of flambe was more than just a theatrical trick \u2013 it was a nod to her late grandmother, a French chef who had taught her the art of cooking with flair. For Kimberly, the flames represented the spark of creativity and the warmth of tradition, and she strove to keep that spark alive in every dish she created.",
